    "title": "Man arrested after shooting kills Mississippi woman, critically injures two others in drug dispute - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By Magnolia State Live ,\n1 days ago A Monday night shooting left a 19-year-old woman dead and two others critically injured following a narcotics dispute, officials said.\nGulfport police responded to the intersection of 20th Street and 32nd Avenue around 8:45 p.m. Harrison County Coroner Brian Switzer identified the deceased victim as Nykel Poole of Gulfport, who was pronounced dead at the scene from a gunshot wound. Two other victims were hospitalized in critical condition—one airlifted and another transported by ambulance.\nOn Tuesday morning, the Gulfport Police Department announced the arrest of 34-year-old John Gaddis III. Detectives determined the shooting stemmed from an ongoing drug dispute between Gaddis and one of the victims.\nGaddis was apprehended without incident a short time later. He is currently held at the Harrison County Adult Detention Center on a $2 million bond, facing charges of first-degree murder and two counts of aggravated assault.\n2",
    "summary": "By Magnolia State Live , 1 days ago A Monday night shooting left a 19-year-old woman dead and two others critically injured following a narcotics dispute, officials said. Gulfport police responded to the intersection of 20th Street and 32nd Avenue around 8:45 p.m. Harrison County Coroner Brian Switzer identified the deceased victim as Nykel Poole of Gulfport, who was pronounced dead at the scene from a gunshot wound. On Tuesday morning, the Gulfport Police Department announced the arrest of 34-year-old John Gaddis III. Detectives determined the shooting stemmed from an ongoing drug dispute between Gaddis and one of the victims.",
